<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bananagate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1975</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bananagate was a bribery scandal of 1975 in which the US company United Brands, formerly the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-fruit-company">United Fruit Company</a>, was found to have paid 1.25 million dollars to Honduran officials to secure a reduction of an export tax on bananas. The revelations, which followed the suicide of the company's chairman Eli Black in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, led to the overthrow of the Honduran military ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswaldo-lopez-arellano">Oswaldo López Arellano</a> in April 1975.</p></div>
